{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Starts (or restarts) the PLAN WORKER: kb.plan autonomy on its own thread, independent of the executive's drive. PLAN_AUTONOMY (persisted agent setting, read live) is the only switch. Armed, it steps the next eligible item via agent.plan.step_item and goes straight on to the next - in-progress before accepted, then board order - so the LLM's latency is the only pacing. With nothing eligible it makes NO LLM calls: it checks the kb.plan facet hash every 5s. Eligible = accepted|in-progress, under MAX_PLAN_STEPS, not parked. PARENT COORDINATION IS THE DEFAULT (2026-11): an accepted/in-progress PARENT (other entries point to it via `parent`) is itself an executable coordination task and stays eligible while ANY non-abandoned child is unfinished (proposed/accepted/in-progress/blocked) - its step_item turn promotes the next child to accepted (or re-accepts a blocked child with a written remedy) and yields IN_PROGRESS; the old `open_children > 0` exclusion and the auto-complete-on-last-child rollup are gone, so the parent also gets the closing verified-DONE turn after its children finish. The park fingerprint includes the lifecycles of an entry's children, so a coordinator's OWN board edits never wake it an extra time while a child's completion or a human's mid-turn move does. Items in the `blocked` lifecycle are NEVER eligible - a human (or the coordinator parent, with remedy) unblocks by moving the card back to accepted. Failure guard: step_failed retries after 5m doubling to 1h, start_failed after 30s, anything else (blocked-but-not-moved, defer_stale, gated, premature_done) parks until a human changes that entry; toggling autonomy off/on clears parking. HUMAN NOTES count as a change: the park fingerprint includes the entry's notes count, and an unseen note newer than the last step's start un-parks a parked accepted/in-progress item. PLAN_STEPS_PER_HOUR caps reasoning turns per sliding hour (unset/0 = unlimited, the default). One step at a time. Idempotent restart via a generation counter; fired at boot by the run-once worker_boot timer. Status: agent.plan.worker_status.","import":"use ndata::dataobject::DataObject;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\nuse flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse flowlang::command::Command;\nuse flowlang::flowlang::system::time::time;\nuse std::collections::HashMap;","params":[],"returntype":"JSONObject","type":"rust"},"id":"houmzl1a164f67b76ncc0","readers":[],"time":1792853069964,"username":"system","writers":[]}